  "details": "The group instances are great. However for some groups, the admins and moderators need a way to better moderate the users in their group and group instances. The inability to do so may prevent some groups from using the group instance feature.\n\nThe Problem:\n\nCurrently, if a user reports something about another user in the group, there is no way to verify if that user was actually at a specific group instance. The only way would be if the reporting user has a video/screenshot of the offence with nameplates on. Though this is unreliable since it may not exist and can even be doctored through image/video editing software.\n\nThe VRCX application would allow a group moderator or admin to log who is at the instance. However:\n\n1. If the moderator/admin crashes, the game log does not work\n\n2. VRCX currently does not provide a way to export these instance logs \n\n3. If VRCX crashes or otherwise becomes unresponsive, it will not work\n\nThe Solution:\n\nThe suggestion is to create a feature where:\n\n1. VRChat logs who joins and leaves the instance (at bare minimum), with timestamps\n\n2. These log files can be saved to a \"group\", where admins can access them, and admins can choose if moderators can also access them.\n\n3. These log files are generated automatically with the existence of a group instance, even if no moderators or admins are currently there\n\n4. These log files can be downloaded from VRChat by the admins/moderators.\n\n5. These log files can be accessed through the website *and* in the game.\n\nThis feature would help admins and moderators manage their groups and group instances.",
